{"game": "escape-from-duckov", "language": "english", "appid": 3167020, "month": "2025-12", "window": 4, "start_date": 1766534400, "end_date": 1767225599, "month_true_total": 1102, "quota": 33, "returned": 33, "pulled_at": "2026-09-26 01:37:36 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "214771007", "author": {"steamid": "76561198796213774", "personaname": "GuiMinero", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/guiminero/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 51, "playtime_forever": 1324, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 401, "last_played": 1777679508, "avatar": "6a180535427ab6a97b44ee99a059aea2ac8111be"}, "language": "english", "review": "Instead of fixing basic stuff like enemies shooting through walls, the devs are sucking the ♥♥♥♥ of a known hacker", "timestamp_created": 1767219179, "timestamp_updated": 1767219179, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 12, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.625747740268707275", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214770943", "author": {"steamid": "76561198884641781", "personaname": "N o V a", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198884641781/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 36, "playtime_forever": 650, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 19, "playtime_at_review": 629, "last_played": 1790376474, "avatar": "a95eee28e6e425bd1f3117da9e094f9f7c21b5ca"}, "language": "english", "review": "Escape from Duckov - ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️½\n\nEscape from Duckov is one of the most fun games I have played in a while. It clearly takes inspiration from Escape from Tarkov, but turns that style into something unique, charming, and surprisingly enjoyable.\n\nThe concept is clever, the progression feels rewarding, and the game has its own personality instead of simply feeling like a copy of Tarkov. It takes a familiar idea and adapts it into something fresh and entertaining.\n\nI would love to spend much more time playing it this winter. It has already made a great impression, and I am excited to keep discovering everything it has to offer.\n", "timestamp_created": 1767219117, "timestamp_updated": 1786396705, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "hardware": {"system_ram": "65291", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900KF", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER", "vram_size": 16045}, "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214763960", "author": {"steamid": "76561199389070589", "personaname": "Rainkenstein", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199389070589/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 4834, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4001, "last_played": 1787626454, "avatar": "1504908089645fa8fcce4a8b1590d6a8318138a6"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is just fun lots of hours in and still just enjoying the game for what it is and offers. Perfect for Dads who are interrupted often to get the kids something or the wife something because you can... wait for it.... PAUSE THE GAME! I know its crazy. Its true though you can pause and that alone is a huge win in my book  for gaming! Thanks to the community too for giving us such great Mods to try this game has changes so much just since its launch I know MORE is to come! MUST TRY IT!!!", "timestamp_created": 1767212318, "timestamp_updated": 1767212318, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.530434787273406982", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214762499", "author": {"steamid": "76561199618447146", "personaname": "pokdot", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199618447146/", "num_games_owned": 168, "num_reviews": 15, "playtime_forever": 3795, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3795, "last_played": 1767209417, "avatar": "18a83618826891dd83bdc2d6df899cddd72051be"}, "language": "english", "review": "体验一般，内容还是太少，流程整体感觉不线性，有些道具是需要前置任务解锁商品比较好过，但是很容易卡任务，一开始什么都没说然后卖了你就发现搜不到了。近战收益是真低，拉满和黑鸭子对撸运气不好就一梭子被干没了。地图设计的也不舒服，一堆地方围栏强制堵住的，跑个图能打开几十次地图？搞个什么高爆雷结果只能炸炸设计好的几个破墙。一开始以为农村镇是第三个图后面还有几个这种boss图装备啥的，没想到后面就是黑鸭子jlab，要特色没特色，见面就瞎叫。枪的话种类也很少，后面会用的也就那么几个枪。绝大数时间花在收集材料提交任务升级设备还有无意义的跑图。地图上也就那个掩体能被破坏，那玩意到jlab被黑鸭子一枪就干碎了，你说你做个墓碑还能被打碎，其他的为啥不能做呢。", "timestamp_created": 1767210979, "timestamp_updated": 1767210979, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.45433393120765686", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "214762216", "author": {"steamid": "76561197990262153", "personaname": "Mowvak Crantis", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561197990262153/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 10737, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 10629, "last_played": 1767283013, "avatar": "5c53dc700b91e18d2a6514d8799b6b120e861de2"}, "language": "english", "review": "This was a fun game. Hope they add more content. took me about 120 hours to complete the content.", "timestamp_created": 1767210744, "timestamp_updated": 1767210744, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214757904", "author": {"steamid": "76561198043082465", "personaname": "augur", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/bobbonifield/", "num_games_owned": 133, "num_reviews": 32, "playtime_forever": 3398, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3398, "last_played": 1767206935, "avatar": "d5ff90ae073ba5e89555debf1f6db98c589e0371"}, "language": "english", "review": "This isn't an incredibly deep game, but it has an enjoyable loop that gave me a reason to keep playing. Great value for the price.", "timestamp_created": 1767206992, "timestamp_updated": 1767206992, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214755543", "author": {"steamid": "76561198293508140", "personaname": "Catless Kafka", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198293508140/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 9, "playtime_forever": 2521, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2480, "last_played": 1767385754, "avatar": "c0c868e026aa56e31fa1ba9df69fbb3525ab9813"}, "language": "english", "review": "it is really good, but the missions are too many, they limits the guns and ways to complete them, it is nasty. The boring missions like fishing are annoying as well, and we have to complete them to achieve the ending. Beside that, it is a really good game", "timestamp_created": 1767205033, "timestamp_updated": 1767205033, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.523809552192687988", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214753829", "author": {"steamid": "76561198996820784", "personaname": "Lifegarden", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/lifegarden/", "num_games_owned": 139, "num_reviews": 10, "playtime_forever": 3241, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 4, "playtime_at_review": 3237, "last_played": 1789233466, "avatar": "bcef0b9cf08f0dc147f0627d8b0b8cdf3f112e57"}, "language": "english", "review": "they call it escape from duckov, but it feels more like a crow simulator lol. you will build a mound of random crap and you WILL enjoy it.\n\nif you really liked hotline miami and want more, you'll probably like this too. duckov takes that foundation and adds several new elements to spice things up. you're rewarded for firing at enemies' heads instead of blasting in their general direction; you also have to factor in your loadout, ammo types, and carrying capacity. they want you to think tactically -- no extravision or magic one-hit-kills. and obviously it's a looter shooter where you have to plan out objectives and prioritize what you grab, not just killing everyone as fast as you can. it's a solid experience and i feel like i got my money's worth. \n\nthough, there were definitely some annoying parts. don't get me wrong, i like this game, but i hope they make it better over time.\n\nthe biggest issue is the quest system's pacing. you are basically beholden to whatever the NPCs demand at any given time, there's not a lot of flexibility. \n\n=  if a task on the upgrade tree requires yogurt, but for some reason, there's a world-ending shortage of it? have fun being unable to upgrade your stats for several hours! \n=  you killed the boss like we asked? well, now we're making you run allll the way down the map and kill it a THIRD time, even though the thing they drop is the primary objective, and you've already collected it\n=  and don't even get me started on the space storm quests. it only happens once every 10 in-game days. that's multiple irl hours. but wait there's more! you only have half the day (a few minutes) to work on those objectives, which are fed to you ONE AT A TIME, and it's hard to complete without mid-to-late game gear. i hope you like waiting and waiting\n\nthe core gameplay isn't perfect, either. \n\n=  range is very powerful, arguably too powerful. there doesn't seem to be a sweet spot between goofy easy combat (using a scoped rifle to hit enemies outside of their pretty short sight range) and very difficult combat (pistols are weak, and shotguns are basically useless thanks to the comical spread). \n=  enemy difficulty is the same way, actually. normal enemies are very easy because they're stupid, isolated, and refuse to coordinate. bosses, on the other hand, can be a real pain. some of them are such bullet sponges that there's nothing you can do without armor-piercing rifle rounds.\n=  hotline miami has high short-term tension (you die in one hit, and it's a packed arena) but low long-term tension (you can retry the same part over and over). i thought the whole point of this is that the tension is the other way around, i.e. weaker individual encounters but you have to monitor your stats, the surroundings, and the objective if you want a successful mission. the healing system undermines this... medkits are powerful, and carrying enough means that one encounter has no effect on the next. it's either getting killed by a hail of gunfire, or no danger at all.\n\nthere was also the whole controversy about the devs' handling of malicious mods. i don't have a horse in the race, as someone who has only played vanilla, but make of that what you will. not that you'd be missing out on an impressive modding scene. (which is tragic, because this is an interesting foundation and i feel like there's a lot of potential.)\n\nhowever, it was a good enough experience all around that i can see past these flaws. it's pretty cool. part of me thinks that private co-op would be awesome if it was ever added.", "timestamp_created": 1767203573, "timestamp_updated": 1767203754, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.506172835826873779", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214751423", "author": {"steamid": "76561198046754131", "personaname": "Meow 24/7", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/i_have_a_potato_brain/", "num_games_owned": 487, "num_reviews": 17, "playtime_forever": 248, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 248, "deck_playtime_at_review": 248, "last_played": 1766895598, "avatar": "baa5ab66e2b8864c396ee9f21119f296e37b971c"}, "language": "english", "review": "Elephant in the room:\nTried enjoying, soulless cash grab unity project by greedy devs that allow malicious code in workshop. The devs should be ashamed of themselves but they dug themselves too deep to admit wrong at this point. \n\nDifficulty: \nAside from the ethic problems allowing malicious actors to still be present and posting content, game-play can be improved. Enemy behavior is too predictable leaving you knowing how to expect each encounter by the 4th run outside.\n\nThere is a problem with the difficulty settings, you cannot tweak difficulty to where all enemies deal the normal damage amount, and losing gear immediately upon death.  Rather, the devs thought it was a good idea to have \"losing all gear upon death\" only be applicable on a difficulty where the enemies deal 150%+ DMG. Very weird dumb decision. \n\n It was fun for a steam deck game for a short time, but not worth the purchase until the devs fix their massive problems in their ego, and overall more tweaks on difficulty. I dont want the game to be easier, I want the game to be easier to tweak for my own expectations of a extractation shooter.", "timestamp_created": 1767201690, "timestamp_updated": 1767201690, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.451701492071151733", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": true, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214744595", "author": {"steamid": "76561199073810911", "personaname": "。。。", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199073810911/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 6, "playtime_forever": 10258, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 529, "playtime_at_review": 10258, "last_played": 1789742484, "avatar": "3604ac34b47c87e187d151f22aa17e107253ce34"}, "language": "english", "review": "1", "timestamp_created": 1767196044, "timestamp_updated": 1789795083, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.534724831581115723", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1760598013", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "214737733", "author": {"steamid": "76561198050576190", "personaname": "georgepi", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198050576190/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 1174, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 492, "last_played": 1767808862, "avatar": "0d6f04a921853fc9dc017699e478c40cff8d3dd3"}, "language": "english", "review": "You ask me: Tarkov or Dukov?\nI'll answer: Quack-quack (•᷄‎ࡇ•᷅ )\nAnd you'll leave without knowing which one I chose.", "times